  "releaseNotes": "Targets .NET 10 and .NET Standard 2.0; .NET Framework targets have been dropped. A DLL or plugin that fails to load no longer stops the scan: each failure is reported to the host as a PlugInLoadException. On .NET 10 each plugin DLL gets its own AssemblyLoadContext. PlugIns is now a read-only list, the public API has nullable annotations, and the generic type parameters are renamed to TPlugIn and THost.",
